## Why This Is Asked

Probes ability to implement a practical, end-to-end beginner pipeline with drift checks and lineage.

## Key Concepts

- Data Factory pipelines and Data Flows
- Drift validation against expected schema
- Spark MERGE upserts in Synapse
- Purview lineage tagging
- Checkpointing and late arrival handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo drift check
function hasDrift(actualSchema, expected) {
  const a = new Set(actualSchema);
  const b = new Set(expected);
  return a.size !== b.size || [...a].some(col => !b.has(col));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle reprocessing of failed files without duplicating rows?
- How would you validate drift in a streaming window vs daily batch?

## Why This Is Asked
This asks for practical rollback capability in a beginner pipeline, ensuring data integrity and lineage even when schema drift occurs.

## Key Concepts
- Data Factory pipelines
- Parquet point-in-time backups
- Rollback strategies and idempotence
- Purview lineage integration

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-rollback snippet
if (!validationPassed) {
  // restore target from backup
  copy("/backup/pt-20260310", "/synapse/target");
  // record rollback
  tagRun(runId, "rollback");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate backup cleanup and retention?
